          %h3#AsTheAbsoluteCohomologyTheory As the absolute cohomology theory
          %p
            In some sense Cohomotopy is the most fundamental of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theories"} generalized cohomology theories
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Music+of+the+Spheres"}> The Music of the Spheres
            ”).
          %p
            Concretely,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Cohomotopy+cohomology+theory"} stable Cohomotopy cohomology theory
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            among
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theories"} multiplicative cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} initial object
            in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"}> E-infinity
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            there is an essentially unique multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          #eq:BoardmanHomomorphism.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}^\bullet(X)
                  \\overset{\beta(X)}{\longrightarrow}
                  E^\bullet(X)
          %p
            from Cohomotopy cohomology groups to
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
          %p
            Specifically for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi K
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = K \mathbb{F}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            (such as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            over the “absolute base”, namely over the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"}> field with one element
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            (see
            %a{:href => "stable+cohomotopy#AsAlgebraicKTheoryOverTheFieldWithOneElement"} there
            for more):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
