          %p
            %br/
          %h3#complexrational_cohomotopy_and_moduli_space_of_yangmills_monopoles Complex-rational Cohomotopy and moduli space of Yang-Mills monopoles
          %p
            The assignment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi k
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{M}_k
                  \\overset{ S }{\longrightarrow}
                  R_k
          %p
            identifying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
            of number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            with the space of complex-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions"} rational functions
            form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            to itself, of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+continuous+function"} degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            (hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle+space"} cocycle space
            of complex-rational 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"}> Cohomotopy
            ).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "moduli+space+of+monopoles#AtiyahHitchin88"}> Atiyah-Hitchin 88, Theorem 2.10
            )
          %p#Illustration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AtiyahHitchinChargeQuantizationII.jpg", :width => "640"}/
          %p
            This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            replaced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#cohomotopy_in_the_lowest_dimensions Cohomotopy in the lowest dimensions
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            is the disjoint union of two points,
            = succeed "-cohomotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of a space.
          %p
            Further, the
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+space"} empty space
            = succeed "-cohomotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
          %h3#of_projective_spaces Of projective spaces
          %p
            Cohomotopy sets of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+spaces"} projective spaces
            are computed in
            %a{:href => "#West71"} West 71
          %h3#On4Manifolds Of 4-Manifolds
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-manifold"} 4-manifold
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            as
            %a{:href => "#RelationToCobordismGroup"} above
            gives for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            of sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
